// serve-web-spa — PLANNED architecture overlay (docs-migration.md row).
//
// Adds the production DELIVERY of the Web SPA: the API container serves the built SPA bundle
// (static assets + index.html history fallback) over the existing `Tailscale -> Switchboard.Api`
// serve ingress, so a phone browser on the tailnet loads the app from the SAME origin it calls.
// The static bundle is served PUBLICLY (it carries no secrets), ahead of the reject-by-default
// auth gate; the API routes stay gated, and the SPA's same-origin calls are admitted by Tailscale
// serve identity (no token in the browser). Every addition is tagged `#todo`; view ids are
// prefixed `serve-web-spa-*`.
//
// Reuses the `component` kind and the `todo` tag from specification.c4 (permanent overlay
// vocabulary), so this file adds no specification block — it references the base
// `Switchboard.Api`, `Switchboard.WebSPA`, and `Tailscale`.

model {

  extend Switchboard.Api {

    spaStaticHost = component 'SPA Static Host' {
      #todo
      description 'Serves the built Web SPA bundle from the runtime image: static assets by path, and index.html as a history fallback for unknown non-API GET paths (the SPA clean-path requirement page-routing hands off). Served PUBLICLY, ahead of the reject-by-default auth gate (the bundle carries no secrets). The boundary is STRUCTURAL, not a maintained prefix list: all protected routes live under a reserved /api/* namespace (gated, reject-by-default), and every non-/api path is the public SPA — so a new API route is auto-gated and clean paths (/, /new-repo, /<owner>/<repo>) never collide. The SPA self-derives its same-origin /api base and sends no token — Tailscale serve identity authorises its calls.'
      technology 'Hono, @hono/node-server serveStatic'
    }
  }

  // The production delivery edge: the API hosts the SPA bundle the browser runs — no separate web
  // host / Vite in production. The running SPA then calls back over the existing
  // `Switchboard.WebSPA -> Switchboard.Api` edge, same-origin, authorised by serve identity.
  Switchboard.Api -> Switchboard.WebSPA 'Serves the built SPA bundle (static assets + index.html history fallback) over the Tailscale serve ingress — public; API routes stay gated' {
    #todo
  }
}

views {

  view serve-web-spa-delivery of Switchboard {
    title 'serve-web-spa — SPA served by the API over the serve ingress (planned)'

    include *
    include Switchboard.Api.*
  }
}
